-- ===========================================================================
-- Warlock / Demonology: custom spell definitions (200406 - 200424)
-- ===========================================================================
--
-- Second file of the Demonology batch.  Pure `alonecraft_spell_dbc` INSERTs
-- that define the new spells the rest of the batch refers to.  Nothing here
-- changes behaviour on its own -- every spell below is inert until a talent
-- points at it (file 03), a `spell_pet_auras` row delivers it (file 04), a
-- `spell_proc` row arms it (file 05) or a script binds to it (file 06).
--
-- ID allocation.  The warlock block 200400-200405 was consumed by the
-- Destruction batch (Backlash, Infernal Bargain x3, Wailing Soul, Nathrezim
-- Foresight).  This file claims 200406-200424; 200425-200499 remain free.
--
--   200406  Healthstone Surge              1  Improved Healthstone
--   200407  Immolation Aura (Felguard)     2  Imperious Flames
--   200408  Immolation (Felguard, damage)  2  Imperious Flames
--   200409  Demonic Embrace (Demon)        3  Demonic Embrace
--   200410  Fel Synergy (Demon)            4  Fel Synergy
--   200411  Sacrifice of Blood             5  Sacrifice of Blood
--   200412  Demonic Brutality (Demon)      6  Demonic Brutality
--   200413  Nether Scar                    7  Demonic Lash
--   200414  Demonic Lash (Demon)           7  Demonic Lash
--   200415  Demonic Lash (damage)          7  Demonic Lash
--   200416  Fel Domination (Demon)         8  Fel Domination
--   200417  Demonic Aegis                  9  Demonic Aegis
--   200418  Mana Feed (Demon)             11  Mana Feed
--   200419  Fel Attunement (Demon)        12  Fel Attunement (haste only)
--   200420  Molten Fury                   13  Molten Core
--   200421  Demonic Resilience (Demon)    14  Demonic Resilience
--   200422  Nemesis (Demon)               15  Nemesis
--   200423  Mana Feed (owner energize)    11  Mana Feed
--   200424  Fel Synergy (owner heal)       4  Fel Synergy
--
--
-- WHY SO MANY AURAS LIVE ON THE PET
--
--   Procs are not forwarded from a pet to its owner -- Unit::ProcSkillsAndReactives
--   (Unit.cpp:6789) only ever runs for the actor and the victim.  So every
--   "when your demon does X" talent needs its aura sitting ON THE DEMON, the
--   shape spell_sha_spirit_hunt already uses (spell_shaman.cpp:1332).
--
--   Those auras are all cloned from 34947 "Warlock Pet Scaling 01", which
--   carries the canonical owner-pushes-aura-onto-demon attribute set:
--     Attributes    448        PASSIVE | DO_NOT_DISPLAY | DO_NOT_LOG
--     AttributesEx3 0x10000000 IGNORE_CASTER_AND_TARGET_RESTRICTIONS
--     AttributesEx4 0x02100000 OWNER_POWER_SCALING | AURA_NEVER_BOUNCES
--   Spells meant to be player-visible (200411 Sacrifice of Blood, 200416 Fel
--   Domination, 200417 Demonic Aegis) clear those back to 0.
--
--   Delivery is via `spell_pet_auras` (file 04) -> Unit::AddPetAura
--   (Unit.cpp:13746) -> Pet::CastPetAuras (Pet.cpp:2354).  Note that
--   Unit::CastPetAura (Unit.cpp:13770) special-cases ONLY spell 35696 for
--   custom base points, so every amount below is 0 in the DBC and is computed
--   at runtime by DoEffectCalcAmount in the owning AuraScript.
--
--   None of these carry a PERIODIC_DUMMY effect for their refresh heartbeat.
--   spell_warl_generic_scaling (spell_warlock.cpp:376) shows the cheaper way:
--   DoEffectCalcPeriodic turns a plain aura effect periodic from script alone,
--   and OnEffectPeriodic then calls RecalculateAmount().
--
--
-- DIE SIDES AND TOOLTIPS
--
--   SpellEffectInfo::CalcValue (SpellInfo.cpp:431) adds nothing when DieSides
--   is 0 and exactly +1 when it is 1.  Every spell here that receives its
--   amount from a script uses DieSides 0, so the value the script passes is
--   the value that applies.  The talent rows in file 03 -- which do have to
--   render numbers in a tooltip via $s1 -- use DieSides 1 and store N-1.
--








